            <div xml:id="d371">

                <pb facs="0324" n="318" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg318"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.115/620: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-04-22T13:00:00-05:00">April 22, 1939—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>107. The Department has noted that for the first time in many weeks no
                    telegraphic report has been received from our offices in China of new bombings
                    of American property by Japanese planes. It is suggested that you might care to
                    mention this to the appropriate Japanese authorities when suitable opportunity
                    offers.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
